From: Razer Edge port draft
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: don't reinit for a flip while only DP holds the PHY

On the Razer Edge (SM8350) the USB controller uses only the HS PHY, so the
QMP combo PHY serves DP alone. Swapping a USB-C monitor for a PC within a
second, with the second plug flipped, resets the SoC: pmic_glink_altmode's
worker calls typec_switch_set() first, the orientation differs, and
qmp_combo_typec_switch_set() forces com_exit()/com_init() while msm DP is
still tearing down the link of the monitor that just left (HPD low is
handled asynchronously). Nothing is logged; the RAM is not retained, so the
reset comes from below Linux (an access with the PHY clocks gone).

When only DP holds the PHY, record the orientation and leave the PHY alone:
msm DP initialises the PHY on every plug and exits it on unplug, and
com_init() applies the orientation then. With USB on the PHY the old path
is kept.

Found on the Razer Edge (1 Kasım 2026): the reset reproduced with the r10
kernel and with the USB role bridge disabled (dwc3 never left device mode),
not with a 6 s pause between the two plugs.
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index c39ced168..0ada9e496 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4785,7 +4785,18 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
 	qmp->orientation = orientation;
 
-	if (qmp->init_count) {
+	/*
+	 * With only DP holding the PHY a flip means the sink was replaced and
+	 * DP may still be tearing its link down: a forced com_exit() under it
+	 * takes the PHY away from a running DP controller and the SoC resets
+	 * (seen on SM8350 swapping a monitor for a PC within a second). DP
+	 * brings the PHY up again with phy_init(), which applies the new
+	 * orientation.
+	 */
+	if (qmp->init_count && !qmp->usb_init_count) {
+		dev_dbg(qmp->dev, "orientation %d: DP only, applied on next init\n",
+			orientation);
+	} else if (qmp->init_count) {
 		if (qmp->usb_init_count)
 			qmp_combo_usb_power_off(qmp->usb_phy);
 		qmp_combo_com_exit(qmp, true);
